{
  "requirement": "Before presenting, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to apply the revised text the reviews return. Where reviews conflict, for example two reviews that split the same requirement differently, it MUST direct them to reconcile the conflict, and to present as a design question any conflict whose resolution changes what is promised.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has three obligations for the `habeas-requirements` skill. Before presenting, it must direct agents to apply the revised text the reviews return. It must direct them to reconcile conflicting reviews, such as two that split the same requirement differently. It must direct them to present as a design question any conflict whose resolution changes what is promised. The test `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_applies_and_reconciles_reviews_before_presenting]` covers all three:\n\n- **Apply the revised text.** `step_of(SKILL, \"Apply the revised text the reviews return\")` panics unless some numbered Workflow step in the bundled skill contains that phrase. `workflow_steps` parses the steps from `SKILL.md` and collapses wrapped lines, so the phrase is found even though the skill wraps it across lines.\n- **Reconcile clashing reviews.** `assert_text` checks that the same step contains \"reconcile reviews that clash, such as two that split the same requirement differently\".\n- **Design question.** `assert_text` also checks for \"a clash whose resolution changes what is promised becomes a design question\".\n- **Ordering.** `assert!(apply < step_of(SKILL, \"Present each group to the user\"))` checks that the apply step comes before the presenting step. In `SKILL.md` the presenting step is step 4.\n\nThe assertions run against the real skill text, and each fails with a message if a phrase is missing. The ordering check covers \"before presenting\". I found no untested obligation, and no unacknowledged gap.",
